title: Ed's second finding, that the new settles fast where a schema exists, is more than an analogy, because for us there is a schema in the reader and one in the graph.
pid: b7928826-06ad-43b1-ac0b-9ead66a4d5aa
body: |2-
  McClelland (2013) showed in simulation that a network learns new
  information consistent with what it already knows quickly and
  without interference; that is how the theory absorbs Tse and others
  (Science, 2007), whose rats learned a new flavour-place pairing in
  one trial within a familiar layout (both read in summary).
contains:
- 99257530-48cb-484d-8e95-959e02bb174a
- 041e5af8-63c8-489e-9e60-b11117c24ec6
